      "description": "Watch Blackburn Rovers vs Sheffield United highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The stage was set for a classic cup tie as two storied sides met in a high-stakes encounter that promised drama from the opening whistle. On August 25, 2026 , the Carabao Cup delivered a tactical battle that swung back and forth under the floodlights. Early Pressure and Quick Exchanges Blackburn Rovers began the contest with intent, as Dion De Neve found himself with two early opportunities within the first five minutes, only to be denied by the alert Adam Davies in the Sheffield United goal. However, the home side's rhythm was disrupted early on when Yuki Ohashi was forced off with an injury, leading to the introduction of Oladapo Afolayan . Sheffield United capitalized on the shifting momentum in the 20th minute. Following a swift fast break, Thomas Cannon clinically slotted a right-footed shot into the bottom right corner to give the visitors the lead. The \"Blades\" nearly doubled their advantage just before the break, but Cannon was denied by the woodwork as his effort struck the post in stoppage time. Afolayan’s Screamer and Tactical Shifts The second half saw Blackburn Rovers emerge with renewed energy after a series of tactical substitutions. Their persistence paid off in the 55th minute when Oladapo Afolayan produced a moment of magic. Picking up a pass from Ryoya Morishita , Afolayan unleashed a thunderous strike from outside the box that flew into the top right corner, leveling the score at 1-1. As the game intensified, Sheffield United manager responded by bringing on Kalvin Phillips and Callum O'Hare to stabilize the midfield. The match became a cagey affair with both sides searching for the decisive opening, and Todd Cantwell nearly found it for Blackburn, only for his angled drive to be parried by Davies . Donovan Finds the Winner The defining moment arrived in the 81st minute. After Tyrese Campbell saw his effort rebound off the post, Romelle Donovan was the quickest to react, poaching a goal from close range to restore Sheffield United 's lead. The visitors' resilience was tested in the closing stages as the fourth official indicated six minutes of added time. Blackburn pushed forward in a desperate search for an equalizer, but a late handball by Afolayan and an offside call against Frank Vare halted their momentum. Ultimately, Sheffield United held firm to secure their place in the next round, ending a pulsating night of football with a hard-fought victory."
